                <pb facs="0305" n="193" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg193"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4019</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Reading</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 171</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi></p>
                <p>His Britannic Majesty’s Ambassador presents his compliments to the Acting
                    Secretary of State and has the honour to inform him that the proposal referred
                    to in the Memorandum from this Embassy No. 144 of February 24th, was the result
                    of a request from the Union of Chinese Workmen in Russia, which was transmitted
                    in a wireless communiqué from the Bolshevist authorities, and has no connection
                    with that contained in the Embassy’s memorandum No. 57 of January 20th.</p>
                <p>His Majesty’s Government have communicated the proposal mentioned in the
                    Embassy’s memorandum No. 144 to their representative at Pekin, for the
                    observations of the Chinese Government, and they are awaiting a reply from Sir
                        John Jordan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-03-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 5th, 1919</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
